# What never belongs in the deriver's build context.
#
# The third of these files, after `.vercelignore` and `.easignore`, and it was
# the missing one. `services/deriver/Dockerfile` copies the root
# `package-lock.json`, all of `packages/`, and `services/deriver` — so the
# build context has to be the repository root, which means `fly deploy` sends
# the root unless something here says otherwise. Unfiltered that is 4.6GB: a
# 1.3GB `node_modules` the image is about to replace with its own `npm ci`, a
# 1.9GB `.next` from the last web build, and 1.2GB of CocoaPods output from an
# Xcode build that has nothing to do with this container.
#
# Deliberately a deny-list rather than an allow-list. The workspace layout in
# the root `package.json` names `apps/*` and `tests/*`, and `npm ci` reads it
# whether or not those directories are here — an allow-list that let through
# only what the Dockerfile copies would be one `npm` release away from failing
# on a workspace it could not find, and the failure would be a build error a
# long way from this file.

# Every dependency tree. The image installs its own with `npm ci --omit=dev`,
# and a host `node_modules` is the wrong platform anyway: `sharp` ships a
# native libvips per architecture, so a darwin-arm64 build copied into a linux
# image is a binary that cannot load.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output, all of it rebuilt on the other side or irrelevant here.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
dist-test
**/dist-test
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Xcode and Gradle output — see the same entry in `.vercelignore`, which is
# where the 1.2GB `ZXingObjC.xcframework` symlink problem is written up.
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/.expo

# iOS signing material. Already out of git; keeping it out of an image layer
# too, because a distribution key in a container registry is the same key.
apps/mobile/credentials
apps/mobile/credentials.json

# Secrets, in the one form they legitimately exist on a developer's machine.
# Fly injects the real ones as secrets at runtime; a `.env.local` baked into a
# layer is a copy nobody rotates.
.env
.env.local
**/.env.local

# History, editor and platform state. `.git` alone is most of a gigabyte here
# and the build reads none of it.
.git
.github
.vercel
.wrangler
.claude
.agents
**/.DS_Store
*.log

# Zips of somebody's Figma exports, and a standalone Expo measurement tool with
# its own dependency tree and a Python cache.
design
tools
docs
